{
  "id": "T18_59_a_policy_that_governs_again_ends_a_period_from_the_start_of_its_latest_governance",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "7.7.2",
    "7.7.3",
    "7.6.14",
    "7.7.5",
    "9.5.1",
    "9.5.8"
  ],
  "description": "A change story governed from the start by the fixture policy has a directive whose lacquer requirement is outstanding. From Monday 8 June an application policy the reference does not implement governs it, and no end act is recorded for that policy, so the story stays open. The requirement is fulfilled on Tuesday: the fixture policy, which governed the period before Monday, records its own end act, directive_closed at Tuesday, but it does not govern then and the story stays open. When the fixture policy is adopted again from Wednesday, its ending had already held, so the period ends at Wednesday, the start of its latest uninterrupted governance, not at Tuesday.",
  "note": "7.6.14: the ending's \"time is the later of that act's `at` and the instant from which that policy has governed the unit without interruption up to that ending (7.7.3)\". 7.7.3: \"Each end act gives its own policy's ending of the period, and its content does not depend on when that policy governs (7.6.5).\" README section 5, Ending policies: the reference records the fixture policy's end acts \"for every period it governs at some instant\", and \"when the policy begins to govern a period after that ending, the period ends at the start of its governance (7.7.3), which reads report and the act does not change.\"",
